-- Rules of Court 2021 (Singapore), G.N. No. S 914/2021, current version as at 5 November 2026.
-- ORDER 10: third party and similar proceedings.  Part roc2, layer 1.
-- Source: a plain-text rendering made by a converter script from Singapore Statutes Online.
-- It is not the official text, and nothing here has been checked against the official text.
--
-- HOW TO READ A RESULT: see roc2-order-9a.l4 and NOTES.md ("Reading a result: FALSE and NOTHING (roc2)").
-- Every answer is subject to O 3 r 2(1) (roc1): the Court's discretion to order otherwise.
-- The count of a period is O 3 r 3 (roc1).  Two seams: `o 3 r 3 the last day for doing the act` for "within" and
-- "before the expiration of", and `o 3 r 3 the earliest day for doing the act` for "not earlier than".
-- "third party" and "third party notice" are defined in this Order (r 1(1) and r 1(3)); the keel's
-- O 1 r 3(1) "third party" says that a third party is a party brought in by the defendant because an indemnity or
-- contribution is sought, and both hold (NOTES.md, Findings).

