-- src:1032 | then, subject to paragraph (2), the defendant may, after having filed a notice of intention to contest or not contest if required to do so under these Rules, issue a notice in Form 20 or Form 21, whichever is appropriate (called in this Order a third party notice), containing a statement of the nature of the claim made against the defendant and (as the case may be) either of the nature and grounds of the claim made by the defendant or of the question or issue required to be determined.
@ref O 10 r 1(1) (src:1026-1032)
GIVEN `limb (a) is made out` IS A MAYBE BOOLEAN
      `limb (b) is made out` IS A MAYBE BOOLEAN
      `limb (c) is made out` IS A MAYBE BOOLEAN
      `the defendant has filed a notice of intention to contest or not contest if required to do so under these Rules` IS A BOOLEAN
      `paragraph (2) answers` IS A MAYBE BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`o 10 r 1(1) the defendant may issue a third party notice` MEANS
    IF `limb (a) is made out` EQUALS JUST TRUE OR `limb (b) is made out` EQUALS JUST TRUE OR `limb (c) is made out` EQUALS JUST TRUE
    THEN
        IF `paragraph (2) answers` EQUALS JUST FALSE
        THEN JUST FALSE -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "then, subject to paragraph (2), the defendant may ... issue a notice": paragraph (2) says no
        ELSE
            IF `the defendant has filed a notice of intention to contest or not contest if required to do so under these Rules`
            THEN JUST TRUE
            ELSE JUST FALSE -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): the power is given "after having filed a notice of intention to contest or not contest if required to do so" (a time from which the power runs, ruling of 2026-11-05, (a), read like "at any time after"; fork F-O10-3) [marginal-a]
    ELSE
        IF `limb (a) is made out` EQUALS JUST FALSE AND `limb (b) is made out` EQUALS JUST FALSE AND `limb (c) is made out` EQUALS JUST FALSE
        THEN JUST FALSE -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "Where in any action a defendant" is within (a), (b) or (c): none is made out [marginal-a]
        ELSE NOTHING -- NOTHING-kind (silent): a limb is not covered, so the gathered answer is not covered

-- src:1032 | then, subject to paragraph (2), the defendant may, after having filed a notice of intention to contest or not contest if required to do so under these Rules, issue a notice in Form 20 or Form 21, whichever is appropriate (called in this Order a third party notice), containing a statement of the nature of the claim made against the defendant and (as the case may be) either of the nature and grounds of the claim made by the defendant or of the question or issue required to be determined.
