      `it contains a statement of the nature of the claim made against the defendant` IS A BOOLEAN
      `it contains a statement of the nature and grounds of the claim made by the defendant or of the question or issue required to be determined` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`o 10 r 1(1) the notice is a third party notice` MEANS
    IF `the notice is in Form 20 or Form 21, whichever is appropriate` AND `it contains a statement of the nature of the claim made against the defendant` AND `it contains a statement of the nature and grounds of the claim made by the defendant or of the question or issue required to be determined`
    THEN JUST TRUE
    ELSE JUST FALSE -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "a notice in Form 20 or Form 21, whichever is appropriate (called in this Order a third party notice), containing a statement of the nature of the claim made against the defendant and ... either of the nature and grounds of the claim made by the defendant or of the question or issue required to be determined" (a definition that says "called")

-- src:1034 | (3) Where a third party notice is served on the person against whom it is issued, that person is as from the time of service a party to the action (called in this Order a third party) with the same rights in respect of that person’s defence against any claim made against that person in the third party notice and otherwise as if that person had been duly sued in the ordinary way by the defendant by whom the third party notice is issued.
@ref O 10 r 1(3) (src:1034)
GIVEN `a third party notice is served on the person against whom it is issued` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`o 10 r 1(3) the person is a third party` MEANS
    IF `a third party notice is served on the person against whom it is issued`
    THEN JUST TRUE
    ELSE JUST FALSE -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "Where a third party notice is served on the person against whom it is issued, that person is ... a party to the action (called in this Order a third party)" (a "where" that fails, ruling of 2026-11-05, (b))

-- src:1034 | (3) Where a third party notice is served on the person against whom it is issued, that person is as from the time of service a party to the action (called in this Order a third party) with the same rights in respect of that person’s defence against any claim made against that person in the third party notice and otherwise as if that person had been duly sued in the ordinary way by the defendant by whom the third party notice is issued.
