-- Paragraphs (3) and (4) apply provisions of Orders 6, 7 and 8 (other parts of the encoding) by reference, "as if" the notice were the originating process.
-- This part does not restate them: it says which provisions apply, and in what role each person is taken.
DECLARE `o 10 r 3(3) a provision of another Order` IS ONE OF
    `o 10 r 3(3) Order 6, Rule 4`
    `o 10 r 3(3) Order 6, Rule 5(6)`
    `o 10 r 3(3) Order 6, Rule 5(7)`
    `o 10 r 3(3) Order 6, Rule 6`
    `o 10 r 3(3) Order 6, Rule 7(4)`
    `o 10 r 3(3) Order 6, Rule 7(5)`
    `o 10 r 3(3) Order 6, Rule 7(6)`
    `o 10 r 3(3) Order 7, Rule 4`
    `o 10 r 3(3) Order 7, Rule 5`
    `o 10 r 3(3) Order 8`
    `o 10 r 3(3) any other provision`

-- src:1046 | (3) Subject to paragraphs (1) and (2), in an action begun by originating claim, the provisions of Order 6, Rules 4, 5(6) and (7), 6 and 7(4), (5) and (6), Order 7, Rules 4 and 5 and Order 8 apply in relation to a third party notice and to the proceedings begun thereby as if — ( a )
@ref O 10 r 3(3) (src:1046)
GIVEN `the action was begun by` IS A `Document kind`
      provision IS A `o 10 r 3(3) a provision of another Order`
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`o 10 r 3(3) the provision applies in relation to the third party notice` MEANS
    IF `the action was begun by` EQUALS `Originating claim`
    THEN
        CONSIDER provision
        WHEN `o 10 r 3(3) Order 6, Rule 4` THEN JUST TRUE
        WHEN `o 10 r 3(3) Order 6, Rule 5(6)` THEN JUST TRUE
        WHEN `o 10 r 3(3) Order 6, Rule 5(7)` THEN JUST TRUE
        WHEN `o 10 r 3(3) Order 6, Rule 6` THEN JUST TRUE
        WHEN `o 10 r 3(3) Order 6, Rule 7(4)` THEN JUST TRUE
        WHEN `o 10 r 3(3) Order 6, Rule 7(5)` THEN JUST TRUE
        WHEN `o 10 r 3(3) Order 6, Rule 7(6)` THEN JUST TRUE
        WHEN `o 10 r 3(3) Order 7, Rule 4` THEN JUST TRUE
        WHEN `o 10 r 3(3) Order 7, Rule 5` THEN JUST TRUE
        WHEN `o 10 r 3(3) Order 8` THEN JUST TRUE
        WHEN `o 10 r 3(3) any other provision` THEN NOTHING -- NOTHING-kind (list not closed): paragraph (3) names these provisions; the text does not say that no other applies
    ELSE NOTHING -- NOTHING-kind (limited by its own wording): "in an action begun by originating claim"; for an originating application paragraph (4) is the paragraph that speaks

DECLARE `o 10 r 3 a person in the third party proceedings` IS ONE OF
    `o 10 r 3 the defendant issuing the third party notice`
    `o 10 r 3 the person against whom the third party notice is issued`

-- src:1047 | the third party notice were an originating claim and the proceedings begun thereby an action; and
@ref O 10 r 3(3)(a) (src:1047)
GIVEN `the action was begun by` IS A `Document kind`
GIVETH A MAYBE `Document kind`
`o 10 r 3(3)(a) the document that the third party notice is treated as` MEANS
    IF `the action was begun by` EQUALS `Originating claim`
    THEN JUST `Originating claim`
    ELSE NOTHING -- NOTHING-kind (limited by its own wording): "in an action begun by originating claim"; the proceedings begun by the notice are treated as an action

-- src:1048 | ( b )
-- src:1049 | the defendant issuing the third party notice were a claimant and the person against whom it is issued a defendant in that action.
@ref O 10 r 3(3)(b) (src:1048-1049)
GIVEN `the action was begun by` IS A `Document kind`
      person IS A `o 10 r 3 a person in the third party proceedings`
GIVETH A MAYBE `Role in the action`
`o 10 r 3(3)(b) the role taken in the applied provisions` MEANS
    IF `the action was begun by` EQUALS `Originating claim`
    THEN
        CONSIDER person
        WHEN `o 10 r 3 the defendant issuing the third party notice` THEN JUST Claimant
        WHEN `o 10 r 3 the person against whom the third party notice is issued` THEN JUST Defendant
    ELSE NOTHING -- NOTHING-kind (limited by its own wording): "in an action begun by originating claim"

DECLARE `o 10 r 3(4) a provision of another Order` IS ONE OF
    `o 10 r 3(4) Order 6, Rule 4`
    `o 10 r 3(4) Order 6, Rule 11(4)`
    `o 10 r 3(4) Order 6, Rule 11(5)`
    `o 10 r 3(4) Order 6, Rule 12(3)`
    `o 10 r 3(4) Order 6, Rule 12(4)`
    `o 10 r 3(4) Order 6, Rule 12(5)`
    `o 10 r 3(4) Order 7, Rule 4`
    `o 10 r 3(4) Order 7, Rule 5`
    `o 10 r 3(4) Order 8`
    `o 10 r 3(4) any other provision`

