§ `Order 10, Rule 4 -- third party directions`
-- ===========================================================================

-- src:1055 | 4. —(1) The defendant who issued a third party notice must, by summons in Form 23 to be served on all the other parties to the action, apply to the Court for directions, except that where the action was begun by originating claim, such application must not be made before the third party files and serves a notice of intention to contest or not contest in Form 10. (2) If no summons is served on the third party under paragraph (1), the third party may — ( a )
@ref O 10 r 4(1) (src:1055)
GIVEN `the defendant has issued a third party notice` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`o 10 r 4(1) the defendant must apply to the Court for directions` MEANS
    IF `the defendant has issued a third party notice`
    THEN JUST TRUE
    ELSE NOTHING -- NOTHING-kind (limited by its own wording): "The defendant who issued a third party notice"; a scope limit with no "only" (ruling of 2026-11-05, (c))

-- src:1055 | 4. —(1) The defendant who issued a third party notice must, by summons in Form 23 to be served on all the other parties to the action, apply to the Court for directions, except that where the action was begun by originating claim, such application must not be made before the third party files and serves a notice of intention to contest or not contest in Form 10. (2) If no summons is served on the third party under paragraph (1), the third party may — ( a )
@ref O 10 r 4(1) (src:1055)
GIVEN `the application is by summons in Form 23` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the summons is served on all the other parties to the action` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`o 10 r 4(1) the application is made as required` MEANS
    IF `the application is by summons in Form 23` AND `the summons is served on all the other parties to the action`
    THEN JUST TRUE
    ELSE JUST FALSE -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "must, by summons in Form 23 to be served on all the other parties to the action, apply to the Court for directions" (a "must" not met, fork F-must in NOTES.md) [marginal-c]

-- src:1055 | 4. —(1) The defendant who issued a third party notice must, by summons in Form 23 to be served on all the other parties to the action, apply to the Court for directions, except that where the action was begun by originating claim, such application must not be made before the third party files and serves a notice of intention to contest or not contest in Form 10. (2) If no summons is served on the third party under paragraph (1), the third party may — ( a )
@ref O 10 r 4(1) (src:1055)
GIVEN `the action was begun by` IS A `Document kind`
      `the third party has filed and served a notice of intention to contest or not contest in Form 10` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`o 10 r 4(1) the defendant's application for directions may be made` MEANS
    IF `the action was begun by` EQUALS `Originating claim` AND (NOT `the third party has filed and served a notice of intention to contest or not contest in Form 10`)
    THEN JUST FALSE -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "where the action was begun by originating claim, such application must not be made before the third party files and serves a notice of intention to contest or not contest in Form 10" (flat negative, ruling N2)
    ELSE NOTHING -- NOTHING-kind (limited by its own wording): the prohibition is for an application in "an action begun by originating claim" "before the third party files and serves" the notice; outside it the Rule does not say that the application may be made, because the other conditions of the Order apply [marginal-b]

-- Paragraph (2): "not earlier than 14 days after" a stated event.  The two events differ by the kind of action.
-- src:1056 | in an action begun by originating claim, not earlier than 14 days after filing and serving the notice of intention to contest or not contest; or
@ref O 10 r 4(2)(a) (src:1056)
`o 10 r 4(2)(a) fourteen days after the third party files and serves the notice of intention to contest or not contest` MEANS Period WITH
    `period length` IS 14
    `period unit` IS Days
    `period direction` IS `After the anchor`

-- src:1058 | in an action begun by originating application, not earlier than 14 days after service of the notice on the third party,
@ref O 10 r 4(2)(b) (src:1058)
`o 10 r 4(2)(b) fourteen days after service of the notice on the third party` MEANS Period WITH
    `period length` IS 14
    `period unit` IS Days
    `period direction` IS `After the anchor`

DECLARE `o 10 r 4(2) what the third party may apply for` IS ONE OF
    `o 10 r 4(2) directions`
    `o 10 r 4(2) an order to set aside the third party notice`
    `o 10 r 4(2) any other order`

-- src:1055 | 4. —(1) The defendant who issued a third party notice must, by summons in Form 23 to be served on all the other parties to the action, apply to the Court for directions, except that where the action was begun by originating claim, such application must not be made before the third party files and serves a notice of intention to contest or not contest in Form 10. (2) If no summons is served on the third party under paragraph (1), the third party may — ( a )
-- src:1056 | in an action begun by originating claim, not earlier than 14 days after filing and serving the notice of intention to contest or not contest; or
-- src:1057 | ( b )
-- src:1058 | in an action begun by originating application, not earlier than 14 days after service of the notice on the third party,
-- src:1059 | by summons in Form 23 to be served on all the other parties to the action, apply to the Court for directions or for an order to set aside the third party notice.
@ref O 10 r 4(2) (src:1055-1059)
GIVEN `no summons is served on the third party under paragraph (1)` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the action was begun by` IS A `Document kind`
      `the date of the third party's application` IS A DATE
      `o 3 r 3 the earliest day for doing the act` IS A DATE
      `the application is by summons in Form 23 served on all the other parties to the action` IS A BOOLEAN
      thing IS A `o 10 r 4(2) what the third party may apply for`
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`o 10 r 4(2) the third party may apply` MEANS
    IF NOT `no summons is served on the third party under paragraph (1)`
    THEN JUST FALSE -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "If no summons is served on the third party under paragraph (1)" fails [marginal-a]
    ELSE
        IF `the action was begun by` EQUALS `Originating claim` OR `the action was begun by` EQUALS `Originating application`
        THEN
            IF `the date of the third party's application` AT LEAST `o 3 r 3 the earliest day for doing the act`
            THEN
                IF `the application is by summons in Form 23 served on all the other parties to the action`
                THEN
                    CONSIDER thing
                    WHEN `o 10 r 4(2) directions` THEN JUST TRUE
                    WHEN `o 10 r 4(2) an order to set aside the third party notice` THEN JUST TRUE
                    WHEN `o 10 r 4(2) any other order` THEN NOTHING -- NOTHING-kind (list not closed): the third party may apply "for directions or for an order to set aside the third party notice"; the text does not say that no other application may be made
                ELSE NOTHING -- NOTHING-kind (limited by its own wording): "by summons in Form 23 to be served on all the other parties to the action"; the text does not say no to another way [marginal-b]
            ELSE JUST FALSE -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "not earlier than 14 days after" the event, a period the text fixes in its own words (ruling of 2026-11-05, (a))
        ELSE NOTHING -- NOTHING-kind (limited by its own wording): paragraph (2) names an action begun by originating claim in (a) and by originating application in (b)

DECLARE `o 10 r 4(3) an order the Court may make on the application for directions` IS ONE OF
    `o 10 r 4(3)(a) such judgment as the nature of the case may require to be entered against the third party in favour of the defendant`
    `o 10 r 4(3)(b) any claim, question or issue stated in the third party notice to be tried in such manner as the Court may direct`
    `o 10 r 4(3)(c) the application dismissed and the proceedings on the third party notice terminated`

-- src:1060 | (3) On an application for directions under this Rule, the Court may — ( a )
-- src:1061 | if the liability of the third party to the defendant who issued the third party notice is established on the hearing, order such judgment as the nature of the case may require to be entered against the third party in favour of the defendant;
-- src:1062 | ( b )
-- src:1063 | order any claim, question or issue stated in the third party notice to be tried in such manner as the Court may direct; or
-- src:1064 | ( c )
-- src:1065 | dismiss the application and terminate the proceedings on the third party notice; and may do so either before or after any judgment in the action has been signed by the claimant against the defendant.
@ref O 10 r 4(3) (src:1060-1065)
GIVEN `an application for directions under this Rule is made` IS A BOOLEAN
      order IS A `o 10 r 4(3) an order the Court may make on the application for directions`
      `the liability of the third party to the defendant who issued the third party notice is established on the hearing` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the claimant has signed judgment against the defendant` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`o 10 r 4(3) the Court may make this order` MEANS
    IF `an application for directions under this Rule is made`
    THEN
        CONSIDER order
        WHEN `o 10 r 4(3)(a) such judgment as the nature of the case may require to be entered against the third party in favour of the defendant` THEN
            IF `the liability of the third party to the defendant who issued the third party notice is established on the hearing`
            THEN JUST TRUE -- the order may be made "either before or after any judgment in the action has been signed by the claimant against the defendant", so `the claimant has signed judgment against the defendant` does not change the answer
            ELSE JUST FALSE -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "if the liability of the third party to the defendant who issued the third party notice is established on the hearing" [marginal-a]
        WHEN `o 10 r 4(3)(b) any claim, question or issue stated in the third party notice to be tried in such manner as the Court may direct` THEN JUST TRUE
        WHEN `o 10 r 4(3)(c) the application dismissed and the proceedings on the third party notice terminated` THEN JUST TRUE
    ELSE NOTHING -- NOTHING-kind (limited by its own wording): "On an application for directions under this Rule"; a scope limit with no "only" (ruling of 2026-11-05, (c))

DECLARE `o 10 r 4(4) an order the Court may make on the application for directions` IS ONE OF
    `o 10 r 4(4)(a) give the third party permission to defend the action`
    `o 10 r 4(4)(a) give the third party permission to appear at the trial or hearing and to take such part as may be just`
    `o 10 r 4(4)(b) generally make such orders and give such directions as appear to the Court proper`

-- src:1066 | (4) On an application for directions under this Rule, the Court may — ( a )
-- src:1067 | give the third party permission to defend the action, either alone or jointly with any defendant, upon such terms as may be just, or to appear at the trial or hearing and to take such part in the trial or hearing as may be just; and
-- src:1068 | ( b )
-- src:1069 | generally make such orders and give such directions as appear to the Court proper for having the rights and liabilities of the parties most conveniently determined and enforced and as to the extent to which the third party is to be bound by any judgment or decision in the action.
@ref O 10 r 4(4) (src:1066-1069)
GIVEN `an application for directions under this Rule is made` IS A BOOLEAN
      order IS A `o 10 r 4(4) an order the Court may make on the application for directions`
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`o 10 r 4(4) the Court may make this order` MEANS
    IF `an application for directions under this Rule is made`
    THEN
        CONSIDER order
        WHEN `o 10 r 4(4)(a) give the third party permission to defend the action` THEN JUST TRUE
        WHEN `o 10 r 4(4)(a) give the third party permission to appear at the trial or hearing and to take such part as may be just` THEN JUST TRUE
        WHEN `o 10 r 4(4)(b) generally make such orders and give such directions as appear to the Court proper` THEN JUST TRUE
    ELSE NOTHING -- NOTHING-kind (limited by its own wording): "On an application for directions under this Rule"; a scope limit with no "only" (ruling of 2026-11-05, (c))

-- src:1070 | (5) Any order made or direction given under this Rule may be varied or rescinded by the Court at any time.
@ref O 10 r 4(5) (src:1070)
GIVEN `the order was made or the direction was given under this Rule` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`o 10 r 4(5) the Court may vary or rescind the order or direction` MEANS
    IF `the order was made or the direction was given under this Rule`
    THEN JUST TRUE
    ELSE NOTHING -- NOTHING-kind (limited by its own wording): "Any order made or direction given under this Rule"; a scope limit with no "only" (ruling of 2026-11-05, (c))

-- ===========================================================================
§ `Order 10, Rule 5 -- default of third party`
-- ===========================================================================

-- Fork F-O10-1: "a third party who is required by these Rules to file and serve a notice ... does not do so or, having been ordered
-- to serve a defence, fails to do so".  The subject of both limbs is the third party who is required to file and serve the notice, so the
-- second limb is read as applying to that third party.
-- src:1072 | 5. —(1) If a third party who is required by these Rules to file and serve a notice of intention to contest or not contest does not do so or, having been ordered to serve a defence, fails to do so — ( a )
@ref O 10 r 5(1) (src:1072)
GIVEN `the third party is required by these Rules to file and serve a notice of intention to contest or not contest` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the third party has filed and served the notice` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the third party has been ordered to serve a defence` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the third party has served the defence` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`o 10 r 5(1) the third party is in default` MEANS
    IF `the third party is required by these Rules to file and serve a notice of intention to contest or not contest` AND ((NOT `the third party has filed and served the notice`) OR (`the third party has been ordered to serve a defence` AND (NOT `the third party has served the defence`)))
    THEN JUST TRUE
    ELSE JUST FALSE -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "If a third party who is required by these Rules to file and serve a notice of intention to contest or not contest does not do so or, having been ordered to serve a defence, fails to do so" [marginal-a]

-- src:1072 | 5. —(1) If a third party who is required by these Rules to file and serve a notice of intention to contest or not contest does not do so or, having been ordered to serve a defence, fails to do so — ( a )
-- src:1073 | the third party is deemed to admit any claim stated in the third party notice and is bound by any judgment (including judgment by consent) or decision in the action insofar as it is relevant to any claim, question or issue stated in that third party notice; and
@ref O 10 r 5(1)(a) (src:1072-1073)
GIVEN `the third party is in default under paragraph (1)` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`o 10 r 5(1)(a) the third party is deemed to admit any claim stated in the third party notice` MEANS
    IF `the third party is in default under paragraph (1)`
    THEN JUST TRUE
    ELSE JUST FALSE -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "If a third party ... does not do so ...: the third party is deemed to admit any claim stated in the third party notice" (an "if" that fails, reading (a) of the rule of 2026-10-29) [marginal-a]

-- src:1073 | the third party is deemed to admit any claim stated in the third party notice and is bound by any judgment (including judgment by consent) or decision in the action insofar as it is relevant to any claim, question or issue stated in that third party notice; and
@ref O 10 r 5(1)(a) (src:1073)
GIVEN `the third party is in default under paragraph (1)` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the judgment or decision is relevant to a claim, question or issue stated in the third party notice` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`o 10 r 5(1)(a) the third party is bound by the judgment or decision in the action` MEANS
    IF `the third party is in default under paragraph (1)`
    THEN
        IF `the judgment or decision is relevant to a claim, question or issue stated in the third party notice`
        THEN JUST TRUE
        ELSE NOTHING -- NOTHING-kind (limited by its own wording): "insofar as it is relevant to any claim, question or issue stated in that third party notice" [marginal-b]
    ELSE JUST FALSE -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "If a third party ... does not do so ...: the third party ... is bound by any judgment (including judgment by consent) or decision in the action" (an "if" that fails, reading (a) of the rule of 2026-10-29) [marginal-a]

DECLARE `o 10 r 5(1)(b) a relief the defendant claims in the third party notice` IS ONE OF
    `o 10 r 5(1)(b)(i) a contribution or indemnity`
    `o 10 r 5(1)(b)(ii) any other relief or remedy`

-- src:1074 | ( b )
-- src:1075 | the defendant by whom the third party notice was issued may, if judgment in default is given against the defendant in the action, at any time after satisfaction of that judgment or, with the permission of the Court, before satisfaction of that judgment, enter judgment against the third party — (i)
-- src:1076 | in respect of any contribution or indemnity claimed in that third party notice; and
-- src:1077 | (ii)
-- src:1078 | with the permission of the Court, in respect of any other relief or remedy claimed in that third party notice.
@ref O 10 r 5(1)(b) (src:1074-1078)
GIVEN `the third party is in default under paragraph (1)` IS A BOOLEAN
      `judgment in default is given against the defendant in the action` IS A BOOLEAN
      `that judgment has been satisfied` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the Court has given permission to enter judgment before satisfaction of that judgment` IS A BOOLEAN
      relief IS A `o 10 r 5(1)(b) a relief the defendant claims in the third party notice`
      `the Court has given permission to enter judgment in respect of any other relief or remedy` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`o 10 r 5(1)(b) the defendant may enter judgment against the third party` MEANS
    IF `the third party is in default under paragraph (1)` AND `judgment in default is given against the defendant in the action`
    THEN
        IF `that judgment has been satisfied` OR `the Court has given permission to enter judgment before satisfaction of that judgment`
        THEN
            CONSIDER relief
            WHEN `o 10 r 5(1)(b)(i) a contribution or indemnity` THEN JUST TRUE
            WHEN `o 10 r 5(1)(b)(ii) any other relief or remedy` THEN
                IF `the Court has given permission to enter judgment in respect of any other relief or remedy`
                THEN JUST TRUE
                ELSE NOTHING -- NOTHING-kind (limited by its own wording): "with the permission of the Court, in respect of any other relief or remedy" [marginal-b]
        ELSE JUST FALSE -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "at any time after satisfaction of that judgment or, with the permission of the Court, before satisfaction of that judgment" (a period the text fixes in its own words, ruling of 2026-11-05, (a): before satisfaction and without permission is outside it, as in O 9 r 17(1) and O 14 r 1(1)) [marginal-a]
    ELSE JUST FALSE -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "the defendant ... may, if judgment in default is given against the defendant in the action" (an "if" that fails, reading (a) of the rule of 2026-10-29) [marginal-a]

-- Fork F-O10-2: "on the application by summons of that third party or defendant (as the case may be)": the applicant is read as the party
-- who is NOT in default, since a party in default cannot sensibly be the one who asks for the judgment "as the applicant is entitled to on the pleadings".
DECLARE `o 10 r 5(2) an order the Court may make` IS ONE OF
    `o 10 r 5(2) such judgment to be entered for the applicant as the applicant is entitled to on the pleadings`
    `o 10 r 5(2) such other order as may appear to the Court necessary to do justice between the parties`

-- src:1079 | (2) If a third party or the defendant by whom a third party notice was issued makes default in serving any pleading which that third party or defendant is ordered to serve, the Court may, on the application by summons of that third party or defendant (as the case may be), order such judgment to be entered for the applicant as the applicant is entitled to on the pleadings or may make such other order as may appear to the Court necessary to do justice between the parties.
@ref O 10 r 5(2) (src:1079)
GIVEN `a third party or the defendant by whom a third party notice was issued makes default in serving a pleading which that third party or defendant is ordered to serve` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the other of them applies by summons` IS A BOOLEAN
      order IS A `o 10 r 5(2) an order the Court may make`
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`o 10 r 5(2) the Court may make this order` MEANS
    IF `a third party or the defendant by whom a third party notice was issued makes default in serving a pleading which that third party or defendant is ordered to serve`
    THEN
        IF `the other of them applies by summons`
        THEN
            CONSIDER order
            WHEN `o 10 r 5(2) such judgment to be entered for the applicant as the applicant is entitled to on the pleadings` THEN JUST TRUE
            WHEN `o 10 r 5(2) such other order as may appear to the Court necessary to do justice between the parties` THEN JUST TRUE
        ELSE NOTHING -- NOTHING-kind (limited by its own wording): "on the application by summons of that third party or defendant (as the case may be)" [marginal-b]
    ELSE JUST FALSE -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "If a third party or the defendant by whom a third party notice was issued makes default in serving any pleading which that third party or defendant is ordered to serve" (an "if" that fails, reading (a) of the rule of 2026-10-29) [marginal-a]

-- src:1080 | (3) The Court may at any time set aside or vary a judgment entered under paragraph (1)( b ) or paragraph (2) on such terms (if any) as the Court thinks just.
@ref O 10 r 5(3) (src:1080)
GIVEN `the judgment was entered under paragraph (1)(b) or paragraph (2)` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`o 10 r 5(3) the Court may set aside or vary the judgment` MEANS
    IF `the judgment was entered under paragraph (1)(b) or paragraph (2)`
    THEN JUST TRUE
    ELSE NOTHING -- NOTHING-kind (limited by its own wording): "a judgment entered under paragraph (1)(b) or paragraph (2)"; a scope limit with no "only" (ruling of 2026-11-05, (c))

