§ `Order 10, Rules 6 and 7 -- setting aside third party proceedings; judgment between defendant and third party`
-- ===========================================================================

-- src:1082 | 6. Proceedings on a third party notice may, at any stage of the proceedings, be set aside by the Court.
@ref O 10 r 6 (src:1082)
GIVEN `the proceedings are proceedings on a third party notice` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`o 10 r 6 the Court may set aside the proceedings` MEANS
    IF `the proceedings are proceedings on a third party notice`
    THEN JUST TRUE
    ELSE NOTHING -- NOTHING-kind (limited by its own wording): "Proceedings on a third party notice"; a scope limit with no "only" (ruling of 2026-11-05, (c))

DECLARE `o 10 r 7(1) the way the action was decided` IS ONE OF
    `o 10 r 7(1) at or after the trial of the action`
    `o 10 r 7(1) otherwise than by trial`

DECLARE `o 10 r 7(1) a judgment` IS ONE OF
    `o 10 r 7(1) judgment for the defendant against the third party`
    `o 10 r 7(1) judgment for the third party against the defendant`

-- src:1084 | 7. —(1) Where in any action a defendant has served a third party notice, the Court may at or after the trial of the action, or, if the action is decided otherwise than by trial, on an application by summons, order such judgment as the nature of the case may require to be entered for the defendant against the third party or for the third party against the defendant. (2) Where in an action judgment is given against a defendant and judgment is given for the defendant against a third party, an enforcement order must not be issued against the third party without the permission of the Court until the judgment against the defendant has been satisfied.
@ref O 10 r 7(1) (src:1084)
GIVEN `the defendant has served a third party notice` IS A BOOLEAN
      how IS A `o 10 r 7(1) the way the action was decided`
      `a party applies by summons` IS A BOOLEAN
      judgment IS A `o 10 r 7(1) a judgment`
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`o 10 r 7(1) the Court may order this judgment` MEANS
    IF `the defendant has served a third party notice`
    THEN
        CONSIDER how
        WHEN `o 10 r 7(1) at or after the trial of the action` THEN
            CONSIDER judgment
            WHEN `o 10 r 7(1) judgment for the defendant against the third party` THEN JUST TRUE
            WHEN `o 10 r 7(1) judgment for the third party against the defendant` THEN JUST TRUE
        WHEN `o 10 r 7(1) otherwise than by trial` THEN
            IF `a party applies by summons`
            THEN
                CONSIDER judgment
                WHEN `o 10 r 7(1) judgment for the defendant against the third party` THEN JUST TRUE
                WHEN `o 10 r 7(1) judgment for the third party against the defendant` THEN JUST TRUE
            ELSE NOTHING -- NOTHING-kind (limited by its own wording): "if the action is decided otherwise than by trial, on an application by summons" [marginal-b]
    ELSE JUST FALSE -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "Where in any action a defendant has served a third party notice" (a "where" that fails, ruling of 2026-11-05, (b))

-- src:1084 | 7. —(1) Where in any action a defendant has served a third party notice, the Court may at or after the trial of the action, or, if the action is decided otherwise than by trial, on an application by summons, order such judgment as the nature of the case may require to be entered for the defendant against the third party or for the third party against the defendant. (2) Where in an action judgment is given against a defendant and judgment is given for the defendant against a third party, an enforcement order must not be issued against the third party without the permission of the Court until the judgment against the defendant has been satisfied.
@ref O 10 r 7(2) (src:1084)
GIVEN `judgment is given against the defendant` IS A BOOLEAN
      `judgment is given for the defendant against the third party` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the judgment against the defendant has been satisfied` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the Court has given permission` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`o 10 r 7(2) an enforcement order may be issued against the third party` MEANS
    IF `judgment is given against the defendant` AND `judgment is given for the defendant against the third party` AND (NOT `the judgment against the defendant has been satisfied`) AND (NOT `the Court has given permission`)
    THEN JUST FALSE -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "an enforcement order must not be issued against the third party without the permission of the Court until the judgment against the defendant has been satisfied" (flat negative, ruling N2)
    ELSE NOTHING -- NOTHING-kind (limited by its own wording): the prohibition is for an enforcement order "without the permission of the Court until the judgment against the defendant has been satisfied" where both judgments are given; outside it paragraph (2) is silent [marginal-b]

