`o 10 r 8(1)(a) the defendant claims against a person already a party any contribution or indemnity` MEANS
    IF `the defendant claims against a person who is already a party to the action any contribution or indemnity`
    THEN JUST TRUE
    ELSE JUST FALSE -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "Where in any action a defendant claims against a person who is already a party to the action any contribution or indemnity" (a "where" that fails, ruling of 2026-11-05, (b))

-- src:1088 | ( b )
-- src:1089 | claims against such a person any relief or remedy relating to or connected with the original subject matter of the action and substantially the same as some relief or remedy claimed by the claimant; or
@ref O 10 r 8(1)(b) (src:1088-1089)
GIVEN `the defendant claims against such a person a relief or remedy relating to or connected with the original subject matter of the action` IS A BOOLEAN
      `that relief or remedy is substantially the same as some relief or remedy claimed by the claimant` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`o 10 r 8(1)(b) the defendant claims against a person already a party a relief or remedy connected with the action` MEANS
    IF `the defendant claims against such a person a relief or remedy relating to or connected with the original subject matter of the action` AND `that relief or remedy is substantially the same as some relief or remedy claimed by the claimant`
    THEN JUST TRUE
    ELSE JUST FALSE -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "claims against such a person any relief or remedy relating to or connected with the original subject matter of the action and substantially the same as some relief or remedy claimed by the claimant" (a "where" that fails, ruling of 2026-11-05, (b))

-- src:1090 | ( c )
-- src:1091 | requires that any question or issue relating to or connected with the original subject matter of the action should be determined not only as between the claimant and the defendant but also as between either or both of them and some other person who is already a party to the action,
@ref O 10 r 8(1)(c) (src:1090-1091)
GIVEN `the defendant requires that a question or issue be determined` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the question or issue relates to or is connected with the original subject matter of the action` IS A BOOLEAN
      `it is to be determined as between either or both of the claimant and the defendant and some other person who is already a party to the action as well as between the claimant and the defendant` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`o 10 r 8(1)(c) the defendant requires a question or issue to be determined also as against another party` MEANS
    IF `the defendant requires that a question or issue be determined` AND `the question or issue relates to or is connected with the original subject matter of the action` AND `it is to be determined as between either or both of the claimant and the defendant and some other person who is already a party to the action as well as between the claimant and the defendant`
    THEN JUST TRUE
    ELSE JUST FALSE -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "requires that any question or issue relating to or connected with the original subject matter of the action should be determined not only as between the claimant and the defendant but also as between either or both of them and some other person who is already a party to the action" (a "where" that fails, ruling of 2026-11-05, (b))

-- src:1093 | (2) Where a defendant makes such a claim as is mentioned in paragraph (1) and that claim could be made by the defendant by counterclaim in the action, paragraph (1) does not apply in relation to the claim.
@ref O 10 r 8(2) (src:1093)
GIVEN `the claim could be made by the defendant by counterclaim in the action` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`o 10 r 8(2) paragraph (1) applies in relation to the claim` MEANS
    IF `the claim could be made by the defendant by counterclaim in the action`
    THEN JUST FALSE -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "paragraph (1) does not apply in relation to the claim"
    ELSE NOTHING -- NOTHING-kind (limited by its own wording): paragraph (2) takes paragraph (1) away only from a claim that could be made by counterclaim; for any other claim paragraph (1) decides

-- src:1086 | 8. —(1) Where in any action a defendant — ( a )
-- src:1087 | claims against a person who is already a party to the action any contribution or indemnity;
-- src:1088 | ( b )
-- src:1089 | claims against such a person any relief or remedy relating to or connected with the original subject matter of the action and substantially the same as some relief or remedy claimed by the claimant; or
-- src:1090 | ( c )
-- src:1091 | requires that any question or issue relating to or connected with the original subject matter of the action should be determined not only as between the claimant and the defendant but also as between either or both of them and some other person who is already a party to the action,
-- src:1092 | then, subject to paragraph (2), the defendant may, after having filed and served a notice of intention to contest or not contest if required to do so under these Rules, without permission, issue and serve on that person a notice containing a statement of the nature and grounds of the defendant’s claim or (as the case may be) of the question or issue required to be determined.
@ref O 10 r 8(1) (src:1086-1092)
GIVEN `limb (a) is made out` IS A MAYBE BOOLEAN
      `limb (b) is made out` IS A MAYBE BOOLEAN
      `limb (c) is made out` IS A MAYBE BOOLEAN
      `the defendant has filed and served a notice of intention to contest or not contest if required to do so under these Rules` IS A BOOLEAN
      `paragraph (2) answers` IS A MAYBE BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`o 10 r 8(1) the defendant may issue and serve a notice on the person without permission` MEANS
    IF `limb (a) is made out` EQUALS JUST TRUE OR `limb (b) is made out` EQUALS JUST TRUE OR `limb (c) is made out` EQUALS JUST TRUE
    THEN
        IF `paragraph (2) answers` EQUALS JUST FALSE
        THEN JUST FALSE -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "then, subject to paragraph (2), the defendant may": paragraph (2) says paragraph (1) does not apply
        ELSE
            IF `the defendant has filed and served a notice of intention to contest or not contest if required to do so under these Rules`
            THEN JUST TRUE -- "without permission": no input for permission, because none is needed
            ELSE JUST FALSE -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): the power is given "after having filed and served a notice of intention to contest or not contest if required to do so" (a time from which the power runs, ruling of 2026-11-05, (a), read like "at any time after"; fork F-O10-3) [marginal-a]
    ELSE
        IF `limb (a) is made out` EQUALS JUST FALSE AND `limb (b) is made out` EQUALS JUST FALSE AND `limb (c) is made out` EQUALS JUST FALSE
        THEN JUST FALSE -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "Where in any action a defendant" is within (a), (b) or (c): none is made out [marginal-a]
        ELSE NOTHING -- NOTHING-kind (silent): a limb is not covered, so the gathered answer is not covered

-- src:1092 | then, subject to paragraph (2), the defendant may, after having filed and served a notice of intention to contest or not contest if required to do so under these Rules, without permission, issue and serve on that person a notice containing a statement of the nature and grounds of the defendant’s claim or (as the case may be) of the question or issue required to be determined.
@ref O 10 r 8(1) (src:1092)
GIVEN `the notice contains a statement of the nature and grounds of the defendant's claim or of the question or issue required to be determined` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`o 10 r 8(1) the notice contains what paragraph (1) requires` MEANS
    IF `the notice contains a statement of the nature and grounds of the defendant's claim or of the question or issue required to be determined`
    THEN JUST TRUE
    ELSE NOTHING -- NOTHING-kind (limited by its own wording): paragraph (1) says the notice is one "containing a statement of the nature and grounds of the defendant's claim or ... of the question or issue required to be determined" and does not say what follows if it does not [marginal-b]

-- src:1094 | (3) No filing and serving of a notice of intention to contest or not contest in relation to such a notice is necessary if — ( a )
-- src:1095 | the person on whom it is served has filed and served a notice of intention to contest or not contest in the action;
-- src:1096 | ( b )
-- src:1097 | the person on whom it is served is a claimant in the action; or
-- src:1098 | ( c )
-- src:1099 | the action was begun by originating application,
@ref O 10 r 8(3) (src:1094-1099)
GIVEN `the person on whom the notice is served has filed and served a notice of intention to contest or not contest in the action` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the person on whom the notice is served is a claimant in the action` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the action was begun by` IS A `Document kind`
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`o 10 r 8(3) filing and serving a notice of intention to contest or not contest in relation to the notice is necessary` MEANS
    IF `the person on whom the notice is served has filed and served a notice of intention to contest or not contest in the action` OR `the person on whom the notice is served is a claimant in the action` OR `the action was begun by` EQUALS `Originating application`
    THEN JUST FALSE -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "No filing and serving of a notice of intention to contest or not contest in relation to such a notice is necessary if" (a), (b) or (c) (flat negative, ruling N2)
    ELSE NOTHING -- NOTHING-kind (limited by its own wording): the paragraph says when it is not necessary; when it is necessary is for other provisions of these Rules [marginal-b]

-- src:1100 | and the same procedure is to be adopted for the determination between the defendant by whom, and the person on whom, such a notice is served of the claim, question or issue stated in the notice as would be appropriate under this Order if the person served with the notice —
-- src:1101 | ( d )
-- src:1102 | were a third party; and
@ref O 10 r 8(3)(d) (src:1100-1102)
GIVEN `a notice has been served under paragraph (1)` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`o 10 r 8(3)(d) the person served is treated as a third party` MEANS
    IF `a notice has been served under paragraph (1)`
    THEN JUST TRUE
    ELSE NOTHING -- NOTHING-kind (limited by its own wording): "the person served with the notice"; before a notice is served paragraph (3) says nothing

-- src:1103 | ( e )
-- src:1104 | (where, in an action begun by originating claim, he or she has filed and served a notice of intention to contest or not contest in the action or is a claimant) had filed a notice of intention to contest or not contest in relation to the notice.
@ref O 10 r 8(3)(e) (src:1103-1104)
GIVEN `the action was begun by` IS A `Document kind`
      `the person served has filed and served a notice of intention to contest or not contest in the action` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the person served is a claimant` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`o 10 r 8(3)(e) the person served is treated as having filed a notice of intention to contest or not contest in relation to the notice` MEANS
    IF `the action was begun by` EQUALS `Originating claim` AND (`the person served has filed and served a notice of intention to contest or not contest in the action` OR `the person served is a claimant`)
    THEN JUST TRUE
    ELSE JUST FALSE -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "(where, in an action begun by originating claim, he or she has filed and served a notice of intention to contest or not contest in the action or is a claimant) had filed a notice" (a "where" that fails, ruling of 2026-11-05, (b))

-- src:1105 | (4) If no summons under Rule 4(1) is served on the person on whom a notice has been served under this Rule, that person may, not earlier than 14 days after service of the notice on that person, by summons in Form 23 to be served on all the other parties to the action, apply to the Court for directions or for an order to set aside the notice.
@ref O 10 r 8(4) (src:1105)
`o 10 r 8(4) fourteen days after service of the notice on the person` MEANS Period WITH
    `period length` IS 14
    `period unit` IS Days
    `period direction` IS `After the anchor`

-- src:1105 | (4) If no summons under Rule 4(1) is served on the person on whom a notice has been served under this Rule, that person may, not earlier than 14 days after service of the notice on that person, by summons in Form 23 to be served on all the other parties to the action, apply to the Court for directions or for an order to set aside the notice.
@ref O 10 r 8(4) (src:1105)
GIVEN `no summons under Rule 4(1) is served on the person on whom a notice has been served under this Rule` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the date of the person's application` IS A DATE
      `o 3 r 3 the earliest day for doing the act` IS A DATE
      `the application is by summons in Form 23 served on all the other parties to the action` IS A BOOLEAN
      thing IS A `o 10 r 4(2) what the third party may apply for`
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`o 10 r 8(4) the person may apply` MEANS
    IF NOT `no summons under Rule 4(1) is served on the person on whom a notice has been served under this Rule`
    THEN JUST FALSE -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "If no summons under Rule 4(1) is served on the person on whom a notice has been served under this Rule" fails [marginal-a]
    ELSE
        IF `the date of the person's application` AT LEAST `o 3 r 3 the earliest day for doing the act`
        THEN
            IF `the application is by summons in Form 23 served on all the other parties to the action`
            THEN
                CONSIDER thing
                WHEN `o 10 r 4(2) directions` THEN JUST TRUE
                WHEN `o 10 r 4(2) an order to set aside the third party notice` THEN JUST TRUE
                WHEN `o 10 r 4(2) any other order` THEN NOTHING -- NOTHING-kind (list not closed): the person may apply "for directions or for an order to set aside the notice"; the text does not say that no other application may be made
            ELSE NOTHING -- NOTHING-kind (limited by its own wording): "by summons in Form 23 to be served on all the other parties to the action"; the text does not say no to another way [marginal-b]
        ELSE JUST FALSE -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "not earlier than 14 days after service of the notice on that person", a period the text fixes in its own words (ruling of 2026-11-05, (a))

-- ===========================================================================
§ `Order 10, Rules 9 and 10 -- claims by third and subsequent parties; counterclaim by defendant`
-- ===========================================================================

-- src:1107 | 9. —(1) Where a defendant has served a third party notice and the third party makes such a claim or requirement as is mentioned in Rule 1 or Rule 8, this Order applies, with the modification mentioned in paragraph (2) and any other necessary modifications, as if the third party were a defendant; and similarly where any further person (being one to whom, by virtue of this Rule, this Order applies as if the person were a third party) makes such a claim or requirement. (2) The modification mentioned in paragraph (1) is that paragraph (3) has effect in relation to the issue of a third party notice under Rule 1 by a third party in substitution for Rule 1(2).
@ref O 10 r 9(1) (src:1107)
GIVEN party IS A `Role in the action`
      `a defendant has served a third party notice` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the party makes such a claim or requirement as is mentioned in Rule 1 or Rule 8` IS A BOOLEAN
      `this Order applies to the party by virtue of this Rule as if the party were a third party` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`o 10 r 9(1) this Order applies as if the party were a defendant` MEANS
    CONSIDER party
    WHEN `Third party` THEN
        IF `a defendant has served a third party notice` AND `the party makes such a claim or requirement as is mentioned in Rule 1 or Rule 8`
        THEN JUST TRUE
        ELSE JUST FALSE -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "Where a defendant has served a third party notice and the third party makes such a claim or requirement as is mentioned in Rule 1 or Rule 8" (a "where" that fails, ruling of 2026-11-05, (b))
    WHEN `Fourth party` THEN
        IF `this Order applies to the party by virtue of this Rule as if the party were a third party` AND `the party makes such a claim or requirement as is mentioned in Rule 1 or Rule 8`
        THEN JUST TRUE
        ELSE JUST FALSE -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "similarly where any further person (being one to whom, by virtue of this Rule, this Order applies as if the person were a third party) makes such a claim or requirement" (a "where" that fails, ruling of 2026-11-05, (b))
    WHEN Claimant THEN NOTHING -- NOTHING-kind (limited by its own wording): paragraph (1) speaks of a third party and of a further person to whom this Rule has applied this Order
    WHEN Defendant THEN NOTHING -- NOTHING-kind (limited by its own wording): paragraph (1) speaks of a third party and of a further person to whom this Rule has applied this Order
    WHEN Appellant THEN NOTHING -- NOTHING-kind (limited by its own wording): paragraph (1) speaks of a third party and of a further person to whom this Rule has applied this Order
    WHEN Respondent THEN NOTHING -- NOTHING-kind (limited by its own wording): paragraph (1) speaks of a third party and of a further person to whom this Rule has applied this Order
    WHEN `Non-party` THEN NOTHING -- NOTHING-kind (limited by its own wording): paragraph (1) speaks of a third party and of a further person to whom this Rule has applied this Order

DECLARE `o 10 r 9 a paragraph restricting the issue of a third party notice` IS ONE OF
    `o 10 r 1(2)`
    `o 10 r 9(3)`

-- src:1107 | 9. —(1) Where a defendant has served a third party notice and the third party makes such a claim or requirement as is mentioned in Rule 1 or Rule 8, this Order applies, with the modification mentioned in paragraph (2) and any other necessary modifications, as if the third party were a defendant; and similarly where any further person (being one to whom, by virtue of this Rule, this Order applies as if the person were a third party) makes such a claim or requirement. (2) The modification mentioned in paragraph (1) is that paragraph (3) has effect in relation to the issue of a third party notice under Rule 1 by a third party in substitution for Rule 1(2).
@ref O 10 r 9(2) (src:1107)
GIVEN `the notice under Rule 1 is issued by a third party` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A `o 10 r 9 a paragraph restricting the issue of a third party notice`
`o 10 r 9(2) the paragraph that restricts the issue of the notice is` MEANS
    IF `the notice under Rule 1 is issued by a third party`
    THEN `o 10 r 9(3)`
    ELSE `o 10 r 1(2)`

-- Paragraph (3): "before the expiration of 14 days after the time limited for filing and serving a notice to contest or not contest".
-- src:1108 | (3) A third party may not issue a notice under Rule 1 without the permission of the Court unless the action in question was begun by originating claim and the third party issues the notice before the expiration of 14 days after the time limited for filing and serving a notice to contest or not contest in relation to the notice issued against the third party.
@ref O 10 r 9(3) (src:1108)
`o 10 r 9(3) fourteen days after the time limited for filing and serving a notice to contest or not contest` MEANS Period WITH
    `period length` IS 14
    `period unit` IS Days
    `period direction` IS `After the anchor`

-- src:1108 | (3) A third party may not issue a notice under Rule 1 without the permission of the Court unless the action in question was begun by originating claim and the third party issues the notice before the expiration of 14 days after the time limited for filing and serving a notice to contest or not contest in relation to the notice issued against the third party.
@ref O 10 r 9(3) (src:1108)
GIVEN `the Court has given the third party permission to issue a notice under Rule 1` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the action in question was begun by` IS A `Document kind`
      `the date the third party issues the notice` IS A DATE
      `o 3 r 3 the last day for doing the act` IS A DATE
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`o 10 r 9(3) the third party may issue a notice under Rule 1` MEANS
    IF (NOT `the Court has given the third party permission to issue a notice under Rule 1`) AND (NOT (`the action in question was begun by` EQUALS `Originating claim` AND `the date the third party issues the notice` AT MOST `o 3 r 3 the last day for doing the act`))
    THEN JUST FALSE -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "A third party may not issue a notice under Rule 1 without the permission of the Court unless the action in question was begun by originating claim and the third party issues the notice before the expiration of 14 days after the time limited for filing and serving a notice to contest or not contest" (flat negative, ruling N2; a period the text fixes in its own words, ruling of 2026-11-05, (a))
    ELSE NOTHING -- NOTHING-kind (limited by its own wording): the prohibition is for a notice issued "without the permission of the Court" and outside the exception; with permission, or inside the exception, paragraph (3) is silent [marginal-b]

DECLARE `o 10 r 10 a person in the counterclaim` IS ONE OF
    `o 10 r 10 the person making the counterclaim`
    `o 10 r 10 the person against whom the counterclaim is made`

-- src:1110 | 10. Where in any action a counterclaim is made by a defendant, Rules 1 to 9 apply in relation to the counterclaim as if the subject matter of the counterclaim were the original subject matter of the action, and as if the person making the counterclaim were the claimant and the person against whom it is made a defendant.
@ref O 10 r 10 (src:1110)
GIVEN `a counterclaim is made by a defendant in the action` IS A BOOLEAN
      person IS A `o 10 r 10 a person in the counterclaim`
GIVETH A MAYBE `Role in the action`
`o 10 r 10 the role taken in applying Rules 1 to 9 to the counterclaim` MEANS
    IF `a counterclaim is made by a defendant in the action`
    THEN
        CONSIDER person
        WHEN `o 10 r 10 the person making the counterclaim` THEN JUST Claimant
        WHEN `o 10 r 10 the person against whom the counterclaim is made` THEN JUST Defendant
    ELSE NOTHING -- NOTHING-kind (limited by its own wording): "Where in any action a counterclaim is made by a defendant"; the answer is a role, which cannot carry JUST FALSE, and the yes/no twin below, `o 10 r 10 Rules 1 to 9 apply to the counterclaim as if its subject matter were the original subject matter of the action`, answers JUST FALSE without a counterclaim (ruling of 2026-11-05, (b))

-- src:1110 | 10. Where in any action a counterclaim is made by a defendant, Rules 1 to 9 apply in relation to the counterclaim as if the subject matter of the counterclaim were the original subject matter of the action, and as if the person making the counterclaim were the claimant and the person against whom it is made a defendant.
@ref O 10 r 10 (src:1110)
GIVEN `a counterclaim is made by a defendant in the action` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`o 10 r 10 Rules 1 to 9 apply to the counterclaim as if its subject matter were the original subject matter of the action` MEANS
    IF `a counterclaim is made by a defendant in the action`
    THEN JUST TRUE
    ELSE JUST FALSE -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "Where in any action a counterclaim is made by a defendant, Rules 1 to 9 apply in relation to the counterclaim" (a "where" that fails, ruling of 2026-11-05, (b))
